  "reason": "The study reports on the utility of human-induced pluripotent stem cell-derived cardiomyocytes (hiPSC-CMs) as an in vitro model for assessing drug proarrhythmic potential. While it mentions categorizing drugs based on TdP risk and provides AUC values for receiver operator curves, it does not report a quantitative measure of agreement between non-human animal results and human clinical results. The comparison is between different in vitro methods and drug risk categories, not between animal models and human clinical outcomes."
